1.	Make sure the Raspberry Pi is unplugged and powered off before attaching any of the wires.
2.	Attach the wires.
3.	Open the Pi’s terminal and run the following command
	sudo raspi-config
4.	Go to Interface/Advanced Options  Click I2C  Select yes and reboot Pi if prompted
5.	Make sure the I2C tools are installed using the following commands
	sudo apt update
	sudo apt install i2c-tools
6.	Test to see if the Pi detects the wires with the following command:
	i2cdetect -y 1
7.	It is a success if the output is as follows:
 
**Refer to expected_output.png**

If the grid is filled with dashes and there are no numbers, then the Pi cannot see the sensor.
